### gloss essere
used as a copula. to be; denotes absolute time; used with as an auxiliary in the conjugation of other verbs, before their past participle; to exist, there be; being, living; being; being, living, existence, condition; being, condition
### gloss avere
to have; to have (done something); property, substance; credit; belongings; assets; swag
### gloss andare
to go; to be agreeable (to), to be pleasing (to) (idiomatically, to feel like, to want/like) [with a ‘person with feeling’ and di ‘thing desired’]; to attend (school, church regularly); used to form the passive voice with a connotation of obligation or prescription; to enter, to take on, to experience [with in ‘a condition, emotion, etc.’]
### gloss fare
to do; to make; to provoke (a physical sensation); to inflict (damage, pain, etc.) on; to cause or arouse (an emotion); to draw up or enter into (a contract, agreement, etc.); to emit from the body; manner, way
### gloss potere
can, could, to be able to; may, might, to be possible to; power
### gloss dovere
to owe; to have to do something (must); duty; Dismisses gratitude by clarifying one acted for one's duty rather than for kindness
### gloss volere
to want; will, wish, desire, want
### gloss dire
to utter (produce (speech or other sounds) with one's voice); to recite; to say, tell, utter; to say (indicate in a written form); to mean; to express a concept with the proper word in a given language; to speak; words
### gloss venire
to come; to arrive; to manifest itself; to take position; to originate; to ejaculate, to cum; to come to mind; to result
### gloss prendere
to take, hold, pick up, get; to conquer (of a political territory or entity); to take (a means of transport); to choose (a certain route or path); to catch (a criminal, animal, etc.); to catch (an illness); to be beat up or defeated; to get, buy
### gloss ancora
still; again; more; yet, not yet; even; anchor (tool to moor a vessel into sea bottom)
### gloss pesca
peach (fruit); fishing; fishing boat; dip, lucky dip; peach (color/colour)
### gloss legge
law
### gloss leggere
to read
### gloss porta
